    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "And what they call folks that are employed on their own gig gig workers, like musicians, artists, Those folks would be eligible for the funding as well, and it would be extended for all those people. It also includes movie theaters, museums, and venues like that, which we didn't cover before. Also, we've got $20 billion for additional vaccine purchases, $8 billion for the distribution, $20 billion to assist states with testing, and $20 billion for distribution. from existing provider relief funds. So again, that's that help get that vaccine out quickly. We've got some more SNAP dollars in here to feed those people that need to need to be part of the program where they go, they get the schools. As someone said, in a lot of cases schools have actually become food distribution centers during the pandemic in a lot of the communities that are really hard at the That's an increase of 15% for the next six months in the SNAP program. About 13 billion is we'll support our farmers and agriculture sector to make sure they can get food to the market. And then we have fishery textile mill research. Kind of goes on and on and on. Also, one of my favorites is we've got 10 billion for children child care centers. As parents have gone back to work or the zooming in, their challenge with their kids not being in school and being at home. 4 million for substance abuse in this time when people are mentally affected by being shut in or losing their job. 82 billion in funding for schools and universities. 25 billion for temporary and targeted rental assistance for those people that qualify. And then 7 billion for broadband funding and 300 million is for rural Brad broadband and 250 million is just for telehealth. And so those are just some of the details, Jody, that you'll see top line on television, but this is a well thought out bill. There's lots of good stuff in this CARES Act that why it was fought over since last July. I embarrassed that I'm part of an organization that can address a pandemic and a crisis, economic, as well as a life-threatening, faster than we have, but I think we're here today. I hope we're signing a bill and I should be home tonight or tomorrow morning with a victory in hand.",
